Once the library is installed, you can use the following program to control GPIO pin 12.

```cpp
#include <pigpio.h>

int main() {
    // Initialize the pigpio library
    if(initpigpio() < 0) {
        fprintf(stderr,"pigpio initialization failed\n");
        return 1;
    }

    // Set GPIO pin 12 as an output
    gpioSetup(12, PI_OUTPUT);

    // Set GPIO pin 12 high (true) or low (false)
    gpioWrite(12, 1);

    // Sleep for 5 seconds
    sleep(5);

    // Set GPIO pin 12 low
    gpioWrite(12, 0);

    // Sleep for 5 seconds
    sleep(5);

    // Set GPIO pin 12 high
    gpioWrite(12, 1);

    // Clean up
    gpioTerminate();

    return 0;
}
```

This program initializes the pigpio library, sets GPIO pin 12 as an output, sets the pin high (true) and then low (false), and then terminates the library.

To compile and run this program, you can use the following commands:
```
