./gpio_test
```

Please note that you need to have the necessary permissions to access GPIO pins on your Raspberry Pi. You can do this by adding your user to the gpio group:
```
sudo usermod -aG gpio your_username
```

After running this command, you need to log out and log back in for the changes to take effect.

Remember to unload the pigpio library if you are going to unplug the Raspberry Pi, otherwise, it may cause issues with the GPIO pins. You can unload the library by running the following command:
```
sudo pigpiod -k
